## Pattern examples

Use these examples to calibrate your scoring. Each key matches a criterion from the scoring table.

---

### THIN_ACCOUNT_0 — author has 0–1 total reviews
> "Great place, loved it!"
> "Amazing, 5 stars!"
> "Very good service."

---

### THIN_ACCOUNT_1 — author has 2–3 total reviews
> "Excellent quality, will return."
> "Fast and reliable, recommend."
> "Good experience overall."

---

### SHORT_TEXT_EXTREME — text under 20 characters
> "Perfect!"
> "Love it!!!"
> "Top service."

---

### SHORT_TEXT — text under 60 characters
> "Good workshop, fast repairs."
> "Nice staff, clean place."
> "Recommended to everyone I know."

---

### BURST_AFTER_NEGATIVE — 5★ review immediately follows a 1–2★ review in the timeline
> "Absolutely the best, nothing to complain about!" (posted 1 day after a 1★ review)
> "Fantastic experience every single time!" (posted same day as a 2★ review)
> "Incredible team, always professional!" (3rd consecutive 5★ after a 1★ review)

---

### FIVE_STAR_EMPTY — 5★ with under 50 characters, no substance
> "Best in the city, highly recommend!"
> "Excellent!! Very satisfied."
> "Five stars, no question."

---

### SURNAME_REPEAT — multiple reviewers share the same last name
> Jan Kowalski: "Great service!"
> Piotr Kowalski: "Very professional."
> Anna Kowalski: "Recommended!"

---

### GENERIC_TEXT — no staff name, product, price, time, or concrete situation mentioned
> "The service was great and I am very happy with the result."
> "Everything went smoothly, no complaints at all."
> "Very pleasant experience from start to finish."

---

### SUSPICIOUS_NEGATIVE — 1–2★ with thin account or generic text, possibly coordinated attack
> "Terrible, never again." (author has 1 review, snippet 28 chars)
> "Awful service, waste of money!" (author has 0 reviews, no details)
> "Would not recommend to anyone." (generic, no specific incident described)

---

### MARKETING_TONE — reads like promotional copy
> "This is truly the best auto repair shop in the entire region, unmatched quality!"
> "Incredible professionals offering a unique and unbeatable service experience."
> "World-class results at an amazing price — there is simply no better option."

---

### EMOJI_SPAM — excessive punctuation or emoji with no informational content
> "Amazing!!! 🔥🔥🔥 Loved it so much!!!! 💯💯"
> "WOW!!!! Best ever!!!! ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐🙌🙌🙌"
> "Perfect!!!!! 😍😍😍 Absolutely perfect!!!!!"

---

### TEMPLATE_CLONE — near-identical phrasing across different reviews
> "Fast service, professional staff, highly recommend to everyone."
> "Fast service, professional team, highly recommend to all."
> "Fast diagnosis, professional approach, recommend without hesitation."

---

### EDITED_REVIEW — review was modified after initial posting (real signal)
> User initially wrote "Good service" then updated 3 days later with specific details about a problem that was resolved.
> Review updated to correct a factual error about the price.
> Follow-up edit added information about the warranty received.

---

### HAS_PHOTOS — review includes attached photos (real signal)
> A photo of the repaired part with a receipt visible in the background.
> Before/after photos of the bodywork repair.
> A photo of the waiting area showing the actual space.

---

### EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_5 / EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_10 — author has review history (real signal)
> Author has 47 reviews across restaurants, shops, and service providers over 3 years.
> Author has 12 reviews, mix of 3★, 4★, and 5★ across different business types.
> Author has 8 reviews with varied ratings, including one critical 2★ review.

---

### ACTIVE_PROFILE — author has uploaded many photos (real signal)
> Author has 120 photos uploaded across Google Maps contributions.
> Author has 34 photos, mostly of local restaurants and venues.
> Author has 18 photos attached to various reviews.

---

### LONG_TEXT — review over 150 characters (real signal)
> "I brought my car in for brake work on a Tuesday morning. The mechanic, Marek, explained clearly what needed replacing and showed me the worn pads. The job took about two hours and the price matched the estimate. No surprises."
> "We visited with a reservation for a birthday dinner. The starter (beetroot soup) was excellent but the main course arrived lukewarm. The waiter apologized and offered a discount without us asking — that kind of service keeps us coming back."
> "I've been using this pharmacy for about two years. The pharmacist always takes time to explain interactions between medications, which I really appreciate given I take three different prescriptions."

---

### SPECIFIC_DETAILS — names, products, prices, times mentioned (real signal)
> "Asked for Michał specifically, he diagnosed the rattling noise in under 10 minutes — turned out to be a loose heat shield. Fixed on the spot, no charge."
> "Waited about 35 minutes for a table on a Saturday, but the lamb chops at 68 PLN were worth it. The wine list is short but reasonably priced."
> "The Samsung Galaxy screen replacement took exactly 90 minutes as promised. Cost was 280 PLN, same as quoted on the phone."

---

### BALANCED_TONE — mentions both positives and something negative or neutral (real signal)
> "The food was genuinely good and portions were generous. Service was a bit slow but the staff were friendly about it. Would come back, just not on a busy evening."
> "Quality of the repair is excellent. My only complaint is the parking — very limited spots and the entrance is hard to find the first time."
> "Friendly team and fair prices. The waiting room could use some updating but it's clean and there's free coffee."

---

### NATURAL_LANGUAGE — typos, informal tone, personal voice (real signal)
> "tbh i was sceptical at first bc the reviews seemed too good but turned out legit, they fixed my exhaust same day"
> "went here after my regular garage couldnt fit me in. bit hard to find (park behind the supermarket not in front) but worth it"
> "ok so i had a pretty stressful morning - car wouldnt start, called them, they walked me through a jump start over the phone for free. didnt even need to come in. thats just good people"

---

### LOCAL_GUIDE — Google-verified contributor (real signal)
> Author is a Level 6 Local Guide with 230 reviews and 4,100 photos contributed.
> Level 4 Local Guide, 68 reviews, active for over 4 years.
> Level 5 Local Guide who consistently writes detailed reviews across the city.

---

### OWNER_RESPONDED — business replied to the review (real signal)
> Owner replied: "Thank you for taking the time, Joanna! Glad Marek could sort the issue quickly. See you next service."
> Owner replied: "We're sorry to hear about the wait — we've since added a second technician on Saturdays."
> Owner replied: "Thank you for the kind words. The beetroot soup is indeed a favourite — chef will be pleased to hear it!"

---

### HELPFUL_VOTES — other users marked the review as helpful (real signal)
> Review has 14 helpful votes — other users found the detailed description useful.
> 7 people marked this review as helpful, suggesting the content resonated with readers.
> 3 helpful votes on a review that describes a specific pricing dispute and its resolution.

